"""Step 4A.5 dedicated benchmark: direction-invariance recognition.

Locked BEFORE being used to further modify the reciprocal-pair /
elimination-by-other-side mechanisms in indemnification_policy_engine.py
(already implemented earlier in Step 4A.5's Priority 2 pass). Measures
whether the system correctly distinguishes facts that are DIRECTION-
INVARIANT (the policy result is provably identical regardless of which
named party is "us") from facts that are DIRECTION-SENSITIVE (knowing
which party is "us" is necessary), without ever guessing an unmapped
role's side.

Each case is (case_id, text, kwargs, expected_bucket, note), where
expected_bucket is one of:
  "AUTOMATIC"        - symmetric/invariant, must resolve without review
  "REQUIRES_REVIEW"  - direction-sensitive or asymmetric, must escalate

Four required families:
  A. symmetric + unusual role names            -> AUTOMATIC
  B. symmetric + unmapped role names            -> AUTOMATIC (side truly
                                                    can't affect the result)
  C. superficially symmetric but materially
     asymmetric (a later party-specific term)   -> REQUIRES_REVIEW
  D. direction-sensitive clause + unknown roles -> REQUIRES_REVIEW
"""

